  "extraction_notes": "[text-pass] The paper describes a series of (GeTe)75(AgSbTe2)x(AgSbSe2)y samples where x+y=25. Se doping is introduced via AgSbSe2 addition. Doped site is marked as unclear as the paper states Se is located in the main phase but does not specify the sublattice (Ag, Sb, or Te). [figure-pass p1-5] The paper discusses TAGSS materials which are (GeTe)75(AgSbTe2)x(AgSbSe2)y. The abstract and text provide specific Seebeck coefficient values for the base TAGSS-75 material. While plots for Seebeck coefficient and electrical conductivity are mentioned (Fig 7a, 7b, 8a, 8b), they were not provided in the image set. Therefore, only values explicitly stated in the body text were extracted. [figure-pass p6-10] Data extracted for AgSbTe2-family compounds (TAGSS series) from figures and text. TAGSS samples are solid solutions of GeTe and AgSbTe2/AgSbSe2. ",
